# Development-only tooling must not enter a runtime image.
#
# tools/offline_shims/ contains a COUNTERFEIT `sqlalchemy` package (plus fake
# httpx, pydantic and fastapi) written so the test suite could execute in a
# sandbox with no dependencies installed. The shim is backed by in-memory
# SQLite and silently ignores DATABASE_URL.
#
# It is not reachable by accident: both images run from /app, so `import
# sqlalchemy` resolves to the real package in site-packages. But shipping a
# module that answers to the name of the database driver, inside the image that
# talks to the production database, is a hazard with no upside. One stray
# PYTHONPATH entry or one script run from the wrong directory and the API is
# reading an empty in-memory database while reporting success.
#
# The tooling that IS needed at build and run time - tls_doctor.py,
# verify_tls_before_build.py - stays.
tools/offline_shims/
tools/run_pure_tests.py
tools/verify_shim.py

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.pytest_cache/
